> cancel (x^2-1)/(x-1)
cancel (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  = x + 1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> cancel (x+1)/(3x+3)
cancel (x + 1)/(3x + 3)
  = 1/3
  holds where x + 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  ucas: simplify (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
simplify (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  = -2(x^2 + x + 1)/3
  holds where 2x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
factor (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  = -2(x^2 + x + 1)/3
  holds where 2x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> together 1/(x + 2) + 1/(x + 3)
together 1/(x + 2) + 1/(x + 3)
  = (2x + 5)/((x + 2)*(x + 3))
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> apart 1/((x+1)*(x+2))
apart 1/((x + 1)*(x + 2))
  = 1/(x + 1) - 1/(x + 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
